To run adhesion dynamics simulations of trphos or schizonts in a shear flow, go through following steps:

1. Go to the respective directory.
2. To compile, run " make clean ; make" which will produce executable "MAIN"
3. Run the executable with following command
    ./MAIN wall_velocity file_identifier number_of_knobs

wall_velocity -> sets the shear rate 
file_idenitifer -> a number that will be assigned to output files (see below example)
number_of_knobs -> Number of knobs/receptors in a simulation. Maximum number of knobs are 1000.

Example: ./MAIN 0.5 1 500

This will have wall velocity of 0.5, shear rate of (0.5/Lz) and 500 number of knobs. 
The simulation will output three files: data_1.dat (coordinates of vertices), data_1.dump (same coordinates data in lammps dump file format) and fp_1.dat (foorprints data).
